---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const faqSchema = {
 "@context": "https://schema.org",
 "@type": "FAQPage",
 "mainEntity": [
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Why do browsers block active content?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "A script loaded over HTTP can be rewritten in transit even on an HTTPS page: it would defeat the entire encryption model."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "What is the padlock with a warning?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Passive mixed content: the page loads but is flagged as 'not fully secure.'"
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "My images broke after moving to HTTPS. Why?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "They are referenced over http:// and now blocked: update the URLs (often stored in the CMS database)."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Can I whitelist one HTTP resource?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "No: the browser decides. The resource must move to HTTPS or be removed."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Does the CSP header fix it for users?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "upgrade-insecure-requests rewrites subresource requests to HTTPS before fetching: a stopgap while you fix sources."
   }
  }
 ]
}
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Mixed Content Warnings: Causes and Fixes"
  description="Mixed content explained: why HTTPS pages loading HTTP resources trigger browser warnings, the types, and how to find and fix every occurrence."
  schema={[faqSchema]}
 breadcrumb={[["Home", "/"], ["SSL/TLS Guides", "/ssl-tls/"], ["Mixed Content"]]}>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-4 text-sm text-ink-faint" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-accent">Home</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/ssl-tls/" class="hover:text-accent">SSL/TLS Guides</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span class="text-ink-dim">Mixed Content</span>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">Mixed Content Warnings: Causes and Fixes</h1>
    <div class="pd-answer" data-vs="answer">
      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">A mixed-content warning means an HTTPS page is loading a resource over HTTP: the lock breaks, browsers block the resource, and users see "not fully secure." The fix is always the same hunt: find every http:// reference and upgrade it.</p>
    </div>
<nav class="pd-toc" aria-label="On this page">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-accent">On this page</p>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="#the-two-types">The two types</a></li>
        <li><a href="#the-hunt">The hunt</a></li>
        <li><a href="#prevention">Prevention</a></li>
        <li><a href="#frequently-asked-questions">Frequently asked questions</a></li>
        <li><a href="#related">Related</a></li>
      </ul>
    </nav>
    <div class="rich-text mt-8">
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink" id="the-two-types">The two types</h2>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60"><table class="pdns-table"><thead><tr><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Passive</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Images, audio, video loaded over HTTP</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Browsers may display but warn; content downgraded</td></tr><tr><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Active</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Scripts, iframes, CSS, XHR over HTTP</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Blocked outright: breaks the page</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink" id="the-hunt">The hunt</h2>
      <ol class="list-decimal space-y-1.5 pl-5"><li>Open the browser console on the affected page: mixed-content errors list the exact blocked URLs.</li><li>Fix in source: change http:// to https:// (most resources exist over HTTPS), or make URLs protocol-relative, or use a CSP upgrade-insecure-requests header as a stopgap.</li><li>Database-driven content (WordPress posts, CMS bodies): a search-and-replace through the database, since the http:// links live in stored content.</li><li>Re-validate: the console should be silent and the padlock solid.</li></ol>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink" id="prevention">Prevention</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5"><li>Add Content-Security-Policy: upgrade-insecure-requests as a safety net.</li><li>Never hardcode protocol in content URLs; use relative paths or https.</li><li>Check third-party widgets support HTTPS before embedding them.</li></ul>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink" id="frequently-asked-questions">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3"><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Why do browsers block active content?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">A script loaded over HTTP can be rewritten in transit even on an HTTPS page: it would defeat the entire encryption model.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">What is the padlock with a warning?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Passive mixed content: the page loads but is flagged as 'not fully secure.'</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">My images broke after moving to HTTPS. Why?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">They are referenced over http:// and now blocked: update the URLs (often stored in the CMS database).</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Can I whitelist one HTTP resource?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">No: the browser decides. The resource must move to HTTPS or be removed.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Does the CSP header fix it for users?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">upgrade-insecure-requests rewrites subresource requests to HTTPS before fetching: a stopgap while you fix sources.</p></details></div>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink" id="related">Related</h2>
      <ul class="mt-3 grid gap-2"><li><a href="/ssl-certificate-errors/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">SSL errors guide →</a></li><li><a href="/hsts-explained/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">HSTS explained →</a></li><li><a href="/ssl-tls/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">SSL/TLS hub →</a></li></ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
